atepublicradio.org/health/2024-03-21/abortion-aidaccess-ban-self-managed-data","line":20},{"title":"the rate of abortion increased","target":"https://www.boisestatepublicradio.org/health/2025-12-09/abortion-data-idaho-ban-shield-laws","line":24},{"title":"out-of-state providers","target":"https://www.boisestatepublicradio.org/2026-05-05/abortion-providers-prep-for-more-patients-amid-telehealth-uncertainty","line":30},{"title":"data released in March from the Guttmacher institute","target":"https://www.guttmacher.org/monthly-abortion-provision-study?utm_source=Guttmacher+Email+Alerts&utm_campaign=e1e363d89c-EMAIL_CAMPAIGN_2026_03_19_02_10&utm_medium=email&utm_term=0_-e1e363d89c-548148985#interstate-travel","line":30},{"title":"in neighboring states","target":"https://www.boisestatepublicradio.org/politics-government/2024-07-08/roe-wade-abortion-data-increase-out-of-state","line":32},{"title":"can face felony charges","target":"https://www.boisestatepublicradio.org/news/2024-04-26/idahos-biggest-hospital-says-emergency-flights-for-pregnant-patients-up-sharply","line":36},{"title":"35% of OBGYN have left the state","target":"https://www.boisestatepublicradio.org/health/2025-08-05/jama-obgyn-idaho-roe-v-wade","line":38}],"metadata":{"title":"Amidst legal challenges, advocates say telehealth abortions will remain available in Idaho","source":"https://www.boisestatepublicradio.org/health/2026-05-06/idaho-abortion-telehealth-mifepristone?emci=e554d6ac-2f4b-f111-8ef2-000d3a14b640&emdi=929c959b-9e4b-f111-8ef2-000d3a14b640&ceid=110103","author":["[[Julie Luchetta]]"],"published":"2026-05-05","created":"2026-07-08","description":"On Friday, a Louisiana court ruled mifepristone, a drug used in about 60% of abortions nationwide, could only be prescribed in person, preventing it from being sent by mail to patients. On Monday, the Supreme Court blocked the law from going into effect for one week. How does this back and forth affect access for patients in Idaho?"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},